In a previous article, dgo@athens.uucp (26265-nachem) says:

>
>Hello. I received a copy of nethack (3.0j+) recently and discovered that writing
>"Elbereth" (especially with a magic marker) will keep some of the nasties off...
>
>Two questions:
>
>1.Shopkeepers do not seem to be affected, are there other exceptions?
>
>2. are there other "words of power" one can engrave? etc.
>

	According to the WCST spoilers,

	1. No nasties represented by the @ sign are affected by "Elbereth,"

	2. No. I think this could be expanded in later versions. Perhaps
there could be another word that kept only @s away. Perhaps more 
powerful words could use lots of magic marker points, and weak ones
(say there was a word that kept newts and geckos away) just a few points.
Of course, this would give Wizard characters an even bigger advantage than
they have now. As it is, a Wizard can always scratch "Elbereth" with his
athame whenever he gets in a jam, and the athame never does wear out.
Perhaps the use of such words would have to be restricted to characters
who have actually learned them in the game, that is, who have heard of
them from an Oracle, Priest[ess], or from their deities, and not from
newsgroups or spoiler files.

	Incedentally, if you have some means of levitating over the
floor where "Elbereth" is written, the writing, and hence your
protection, will last indefinitely, provided you used some reasonably
permanent method of writing (magic marker, athame, wand of digging, etc).

